#
# A fling is never throttled with the offscreen animations (patch 0001).
#
# On the scrolling thread LayerTreeHost::requestComposition() forwards a
# fling step only when that thread flagged a layer change, and during
# flings on some pages the flag stays unset: the step is applied but shown
# only by the next composite for another reason. With an animation on
# screen that is every frame; once Wikipedia's header (and its pulsating
# dot) has scrolled away, patch 0001 ticked those composites at 10 Hz and
# flings ran at 10 frames a second on the Jolla Phone. The scrolling thread
# now notes every step: the compositor does not throttle within 250 ms of
# one, and a step that arrives while it does is composited at once.
#
